ecil 1.2 features=0x0000000a
; C++: covariant results.  C::Two() returns C* and C::Three() returns C& for
;   B *B::Two(); B &B::Three(); (C : A, B, so B is at offset 8).  The pointer
; result keeps a null (not adjusted), the reference result is adjusted even when
; it is a (bogus) null reference: CLASS_VFUNCS flag REF_RESULT (0x08).  The
; stream is the ECIL writer's output with REF_RESULT added by hand.
; RUN: %ecil-asm %s -o %t.ecil
; RUN: %edg-cir --emit=cir %t.ecil | %FileCheck %s
; RUN: %edg-cir --emit=obj -o %t.o %t.ecil
; RUN: g++ %t.o -o %t.exe
; RUN: %t.exe

; CHECK-LABEL: cir.func {{.*}}@_ZTchn8_h8_N1C3TwoEv
; CHECK: cir.ternary
; CHECK-LABEL: cir.func {{.*}}@_ZTchn8_h8_N1C5ThreeEv
; CHECK-NOT: cir.ternary
; CHECK: cir.return

